#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068922 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068584 :question/id #uuid "f374b567-9a69-57ae-88eb-644ebfc451d7" :question/math-academy-id "e-506" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int  \\dfrac{5x}{x^2+3x-4} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\nx^2+3x-4 = (x-1)(x+4) \\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x}{{x}^{2}+3x-4} & =\\frac{5x}{(x-1)(x+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{A}{(x-1)}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =A(x+4)+B(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-4) & =A(-4+4)+B(-4-1) \\\\ -20 & =-5B \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, by plugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1) & =A(1+4)+B(1-1) \\\\ 5 & =5A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x}{x^2+3x-4}  = \\dfrac{1}{(x-1)} +\\dfrac{4}{(x+4)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x}{{x}^{2}+3x-4}\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{4}{x+4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\text{d}x+4\\int \\frac{1}{x+4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54bab77-d77f-5275-b454-ddb565eaa280" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048375 :topic/math-academy-id 372 :topic/title "Factoring Trinomials With Leading Coefficients"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048557 :topic/math-academy-id 331 :topic/title "Integrating Linear Rational Functions Using Substitution"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049195 :topic/math-academy-id 30 :topic/title "Combining the Laws of Logarithms"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050050 :topic/math-academy-id 1060 :topic/title "Expressing Rational Functions as Sums of Partial Fractions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24ae7afd-8576-5602-9501-9c611ec3ed70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330263} {:answer/id #uuid "4201b9e5-4180-5325-b8c7-2805b2c0f988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330537} {:answer/id #uuid "7739fe2a-f91d-523e-b519-5eba915ac6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331016} {:answer/id #uuid "acecead2-9843-5d76-95c9-05999fbf5f2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331483} {:answer/id #uuid "eb610479-69f3-5893-b5aa-5c24f871f951" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24ae7afd-8576-5602-9501-9c611ec3ed70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330263} :answer-field/id #uuid "a49e43bf-f0bc-5e97-9fad-8508bb19da5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332489}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f6ebcba-4e39-5954-8ee8-c37c592d0f6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-49604" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x=a\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+b\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C,\n$$\n\nfind the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)} & =\\frac{A}{3x+2}+\\frac{B}{2x-3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n13=A(2x-3)+B(3x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & =A(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+B(3(\\frac{3}{2})+2) \\\\ 13 & =\\frac{13}{2}B \\\\ B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{2}{3},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & =A(2(-\\frac{2}{3})-3)+B(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2) \\\\ 13 & =-\\frac{13}{3}A \\\\ A & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}=-\\frac{3}{3x+2}+\\frac{2}{2x-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{3}{3x+2}+\\frac{2}{2x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{3}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=1,b=-1,$ and $a+b=1-1=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8294469-b10f-5558-b3dc-de74f0bf019b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}x & -\\frac{1}{5}\\ln & x - 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067547} {:answer/id #uuid "f355ef9f-48e7-54fc-8ccf-5ff5b25fabf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}x & -\\frac{1}{5}\\ln & x - 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067548} {:answer/id #uuid "14624ca2-6eee-5d13-acad-913c3ca49068" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}x & -5\\ln & x - 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067549} {:answer/id #uuid "2e883ada-9680-5bb3-be9b-032307e720ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}x & -\\ln & x - 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067550} {:answer/id #uuid "35e6c592-3ab9-5f4b-b411-afed57d71194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}x & -5\\ln & x - 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067551}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5839c2f2-20f1-5376-86e6-f1fb928b1eab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067546}] :question/id #uuid "f29adfb1-f6e4-5efe-acf8-fa2f7f98e7f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-49904" :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int(-5)/(x(x - 1))dx$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71cce186-30b6-55d0-84d4-342f5c753f10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71cce186-30b6-55d0-84d4-342f5c753f10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234716} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ae52c6e-7b2f-5af5-8b96-5d84295d8e11" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235015} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1e90155-6ac0-50f6-a4fb-8e3b6bbb20ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1e90155-6ac0-50f6-a4fb-8e3b6bbb20ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234928} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6edf15-5a56-5db4-8849-32a5330ee399" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235030}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "333f44c6-e7aa-5f32-a7e4-9a58be270016" :question/math-academy-id "q-128339" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=A{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x-3}+B{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}x}{2x+1}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are constants, find $A$ and $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $B=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator and denominator of $f(x)$:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{7}{2{x}^{2}-5x-3}=\\frac{7}{(x-3)(2x+1)}\n$$\n\nOur task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(2x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n7=A(2x+1)+B(x-3).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =A(2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+1)+B(-\\frac{1}{2}-3) \\\\ 7 & =-\\frac{7}{2}B \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =A(2\\cdot 3+1)+B(3-3) \\\\ 7 & =7A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x-3}-\\frac{2}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }(\\frac{1}{x-3}-\\frac{2}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x-3}-2{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}x}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $A=1$ and $B=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "036e519f-c924-5649-b208-3cae45c9c3c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238111} {:answer/id #uuid "60b2f004-1b0a-52b0-9b2b-ebdac2ed1485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238905} {:answer/id #uuid "8e197d1b-f46a-5bca-b996-28be90359d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239289} {:answer/id #uuid "9f7cf41d-bf13-5501-a648-617b7fb48f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239447} {:answer/id #uuid "c228a57c-3a58-5cc8-9d7b-d801859aadae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c228a57c-3a58-5cc8-9d7b-d801859aadae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239758} :answer-field/id #uuid "39c03836-aefa-5c2d-a5b3-6de207664cbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240431}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed315823-9912-53f6-ae66-2685405a1454" :question/math-academy-id "q-103988" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2x+7}{(2x+1)(x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+7}{(2x+1)(x+2)} & =\\frac{A}{2x+1}+\\frac{B}{x+2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2x+7=A(x+2)+B(2x+1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)+7 & =A((-2)+2)+B(2(-2)+1) \\\\ 3 & =-3B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-\\frac{1}{2})+7 & =A(-\\frac{1}{2}+2)+B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\ 6 & =A(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+7}{(2x+1)(x+2)} & =\\frac{4}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+7}{(2x+1)(x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021f6895-433e-546e-8a64-b6694c9f9037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238097} {:answer/id #uuid "17632347-1091-5700-9637-3abb325c6ed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238256} {:answer/id #uuid "27e3c466-6f7a-56cd-9dc3-54816a11c3c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238402} {:answer/id #uuid "83738b98-16d3-528c-b36c-5c5b3a4b4e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239199} {:answer/id #uuid "f85a7627-23df-52ea-bb89-b64fab1c596d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f85a7627-23df-52ea-bb89-b64fab1c596d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240252} :answer-field/id #uuid "50cdad8b-c02c-55a4-9c4c-8f85dc88ae18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240474}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "992496e6-fae7-5b47-9d13-a4fe5d22fb68" :question/math-academy-id "q-103989" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)} & =\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2x-4=A(x-4)+Bx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(4)-4 & =A(4-4)+B(4) \\\\ 4 & =4B \\\\ 1 & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)-4 & =A(0-4)+B(0) \\\\ -4 & =-4A \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)} & =\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a64c7100-7ebf-5dc1-a9ef-5db761aa5ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a64c7100-7ebf-5dc1-a9ef-5db761aa5ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318137} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d8ecaab-2fb2-5e35-84b4-1bc548395ce7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318454} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20c5029e-f1d7-5010-830c-c488b9a19a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20c5029e-f1d7-5010-830c-c488b9a19a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317667} :answer-field/id #uuid "f44b667a-5e64-5e0e-992c-ccb90e018822" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318930}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e9f94ca-0527-57ee-8929-045d95cec1a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-348896" :question/problem "Evaluate the following indefinite integral and fill in the missing coefficients.\n\n$\\int \\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+3)(x-4).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)} & =\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n7x+7=A(x-4)+B(x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(4)+7 & =A(4-4)+B(4+3) \\\\ 35 & =7B \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-3)+7 & =A(-3-4)+B(-3+3) \\\\ -14 & =-7A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}=\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{5}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+5\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+5\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fee16e3e-8324-5543-ac59-909d500e4767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fee16e3e-8324-5543-ac59-909d500e4767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318418} :answer-field/id #uuid "10717b08-03cd-5ded-bf16-282dd967767d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318460} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "191068f5-0226-522d-8139-273589d252a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "191068f5-0226-522d-8139-273589d252a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317644} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a285674-48f7-5a5c-8bd3-25042027da0c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318480}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d366a4f-57bf-550b-968a-5c4e774413e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-348898" :question/problem "Evaluate the following indefinite integral and fill in the missing coefficients.\n\n$\\int \\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-8|\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x-8)(x+1).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{x-8}+\\frac{B}{x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n7x-11=A(x+1)+B(x-8).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=8,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(8)-11 & =A(8+1)+B(8-8) \\\\ 45 & =9A \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-1)-11 & =A(-1+1)+B(-1-8) \\\\ -18 & =-9B \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)}=\\frac{5}{x-8}+\\frac{2}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{1}{x-8}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-8|+2\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af7b29aa-b092-5da7-b4e9-45228ee68f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af7b29aa-b092-5da7-b4e9-45228ee68f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318159} :answer-field/id #uuid "847e26e5-c13c-5b78-ba77-53e00e7a5563" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318710} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d37eb2c0-6560-554b-bcb1-022f29baa596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d37eb2c0-6560-554b-bcb1-022f29baa596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318266} :answer-field/id #uuid "8564b54b-4b86-5672-8a6f-ba009a7f5474" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318712}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d78f678c-271e-5e6f-bc0e-d0b4c96c7b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-348933" :question/problem "Evaluate the following indefinite integral and fill in the missing coefficients.\n\n$\\int \\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+5|\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n(2x+5)(x-2).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)} & =\\frac{A}{2x+5}+\\frac{B}{x-2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n11=A(x-2)+B(2x+5).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11 & =9B \\\\ B & =\\frac{11}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{5}{2},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11 & =-\\frac{9}{2}A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{22}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)}=-\\frac{22}{9(2x+5)}+\\frac{11}{9(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{22}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{11}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{9}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+5|+\\frac{11}{9}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332785 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3093957e-b600-549a-aa94-f6eff16fa62b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330378} {:answer/id #uuid "446fd5ce-d55b-5bca-8c08-7bebb04c4c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330564} {:answer/id #uuid "57610450-810b-53cd-b769-0eeb48828a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330732} {:answer/id #uuid "990e7f87-f46f-5c57-8462-75c680e07388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331318} {:answer/id #uuid "c40af496-e35d-5592-a703-fa0cf0ade2d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3093957e-b600-549a-aa94-f6eff16fa62b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330378} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bfb35c2-169d-522b-a184-a7dabe1884ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332241}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d10b74c-0855-5f3d-9ce9-b42a8bd557bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-49903" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{6x+12}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x+12}{x(x+3)} & =\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x+3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n6x+12=A(x+3)+Bx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(-3)+12 & =A(-3+3)+B(-3) \\\\ -6 & =-3B \\\\ B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)+12 & =A(0+3)+B(0) \\\\ 12 & =3A \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x+12}{x(x+3)}=\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{2}{x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6x+12}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{2}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8eb71edc-1611-5574-8e7e-8f7b3936ff0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331213} {:answer/id #uuid "97f1817a-04e4-55bd-9d46-5de306b15c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331304} {:answer/id #uuid "abcc04b6-41a0-58ce-94e2-8537295db75a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331475} {:answer/id #uuid "c490eb1b-6330-524a-a5e4-555370670a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331697} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc8d2f7-7152-57db-b954-c96f6cb2f941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c490eb1b-6330-524a-a5e4-555370670a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331697} :answer-field/id #uuid "15871e44-ae83-5585-90d9-a66f6aac88ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332228}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2807863a-263b-547c-96e7-4e784ccb6278" :question/math-academy-id "q-49905" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{5x-1}{(x-3)(2x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x=a\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+b\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+C,\n$$\n\nfind the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-1}{(x-3)(2x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{2x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n5x-1=A(2x+1)+B(x-3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-\\frac{1}{2})-1 & =A(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)+B(-\\frac{1}{2}-3) \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} & =-\\frac{7}{2}B \\\\ B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)-1 & =A(2(3)+1)+B(3-3) \\\\ 14 & =7A \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-1}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{1}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x-1}{(x-3)(2x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{1}{2x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{2}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=2,b=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $a+b=2+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bfc3304-e547-5d93-85cf-d63b46ad634d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330197} {:answer/id #uuid "945ced1f-8fea-5c1d-a75d-ca4b571df7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331265} {:answer/id #uuid "b3053017-09aa-5c07-8524-e09690ea6055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331530} {:answer/id #uuid "bf976cda-48d5-50b8-89c7-c7fb49822dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331648} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc85048-9121-59e1-9a1e-20b6d9412725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf976cda-48d5-50b8-89c7-c7fb49822dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331648} :answer-field/id #uuid "54e3b30d-0abd-511a-a133-4c34869bac9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332361}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b4836967-af93-5f43-b351-fdcfbef30921" :question/math-academy-id "q-49908" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2}{3{x}^{2}+x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}+x=x(3x+1).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{x(3x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{(3x+1)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2=A(3x+1)+Bx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{3},$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A(3(-\\frac{1}{3})+1)+B(-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ 2 & =-\\frac{1}{3}B \\\\ 6 & =-B \\\\ B & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A(3(0)+1)+B(0) \\\\ 2 & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{x(3x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{6}{3x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x(3x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{6}{3x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{3}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ec330cc-8c77-5e4b-b2b9-ffed05aa242e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397789} {:answer/id #uuid "7c0961d6-77ee-5ef6-b56f-f97f7519ca2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397790} {:answer/id #uuid "67f68e51-f432-57bf-9c04-5cee503b7449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397791} {:answer/id #uuid "297fec68-7633-5a4f-b758-461f512bfa1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397792} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7e14f3-bd1f-5912-9586-f5fdac2f41f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67f68e51-f432-57bf-9c04-5cee503b7449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397791} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdede32f-8b30-513b-878d-48ae1f1b992d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397788}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8d217e5-8474-5d6b-93f2-6f6e1253c6f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-103991" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{7}{(x-1)(x+6)}\\,\\text{d}x=a\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+b\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+6|+C,\n$$\n\nfind the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{(x-1)(x+6)} & =\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+6},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n7=A(x+6)+B(x-1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-6,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =A(-6+6)+B(-6-1) \\\\ 7 & =-7B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =A(1+6)+B(1-1) \\\\ 7 & =7A \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{(x-1)(x+6)} & =\\frac{1}{x-1}-\\frac{1}{x+6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7}{(x-1)(x+6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x-1}-\\frac{1}{x+6})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+6|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=1,b=-1,$ and $a+b=1-1=0.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Indefinite Integral of a Rational Function Using Partial Fractions"}]}
